---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const locale = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security & Privacy — Verified Controls for Your Business Data"
  description="Kraal Code's security architecture covers tenant isolation, RBAC, immutable audit trails, AES-256 encryption, MFA, and OWASP Top 10 mapping. Visit our Trust Centre."
  locale={locale}
  canonicalUrl="https://kraalcode.com/en/security/"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Security that enables your operations</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-subtext">Security and privacy are not afterthoughts. They are what makes remote work, branch operations, cloud access, and global collaboration possible without abandoning accountability.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container security-grid">
      <div class="security-image">
        <img src="/src/assets/images/security/security-cloud-tablet-globe.jpg" alt="Cloud security concept with tablet showing global data protection" width="560" height="400" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="security-content">
        <h2>How Kraal Code protects your organisation</h2>
        <p>Every design decision in Kraal Code starts from a security question: who can see this, who can do this, and how is it recorded? The answers shape every module, every workflow, and every permission.</p>
        <p>These are verified controls from the product's security architecture — not marketing promises.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--warm section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Verified Security Controls</h2>
      <div class="controls-grid">
        <div class="control-card">
          <h3>Tenant Isolation</h3>
          <p>Every organisation's data is isolated at the database level using row-level tenant isolation. The tenant ID comes exclusively from the server-side session — never from request parameters. Cross-tenant access returns HTTP 404 to prevent enumeration.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control-card">
          <h3>Role-Based Access Control</h3>
          <p>Unlimited roles with granular permissions, branch restrictions, and approval limits. Control who can create, approve, view, and export every type of record. Segregation of duties enforced by design.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control-card">
          <h3>Immutable Audit Trail</h3>
          <p>Every action — create, read, update, delete, approval, login, logout, role change — is recorded in an INSERT-only log. No one can alter or delete audit records. 7-year retention. External auditor read-only role available.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control-card">
          <h3>Encryption</h3>
          <p>TLS 1.3 for all traffic in transit. AES-256 encryption at rest for sensitive data: salary information, national IDs, bank account numbers, biometric identifiers. Bcrypt (cost ≥ 12) for passwords. Database backups encrypted.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control-card">
          <h3>Multi-Factor Authentication</h3>
          <p>TOTP-based two-factor authentication (NIST SP 800-63B AAL2). Biometric login support. Account lockout after 5 failed attempts. Session invalidation within 5 seconds of account disable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control-card">
          <h3>OWASP Top 10 (2021) Mapped</h3>
          <p>Security architecture is designed against all ten OWASP Top 10 categories: broken access control, cryptographic failures, injection, insecure design, security misconfiguration, vulnerable components, authentication failures, software integrity, logging, and SSRF.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control-card">
          <h3>Rate Limiting</h3>
          <p>Token bucket algorithm, configurable per tenant, per user, and per subscription plan. HTTP 429 with Retry-After header when limits are exceeded.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="control-card">
          <h3>Security Headers</h3>
          <p>Content-Security-Policy with per-request nonce. X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff. X-Frame-Options: DENY. Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin. Permissions-Policy restricting camera, microphone, and geolocation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Data Protection</h2>
      <div class="protection-grid">
        <div class="protection-card">
          <h3>Uganda PDPA 2019</h3>
          <p>Kraal Code is designed with controls informed by the Uganda Data Protection and Privacy Act 2019. The platform operates as data processor; the tenant is data controller.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="protection-card">
          <h3>Data Retention</h3>
          <p>Configurable retention periods per data category. Subject access export within 72 hours. Tenant offboarding: archive within 30 days, purge after 90 days, audit logs retained for 7 years.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="protection-card">
          <h3>Sub-Processor Register</h3>
          <p>Maintained and available on request. Consent capture for sensitive HR data. No cross-border transfers without documented legal basis.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--dark section">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <h2>Have security questions?</h2>
      <p>We take security seriously and are happy to discuss our controls with your IT team, security reviewers, or procurement panel.</p>
      <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--inverse">Contact Our Team →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--kc-space-20) 0 var(--kc-space-12);
    background: var(--kc-surface-dark);
    color: var(--kc-text-inverse);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-4xl);
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .page-hero-subtext {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    color: var(--kc-text-inverse-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }

  .security-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--kc-space-12);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .security-image {
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .security-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .security-content h2 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-4);
  }

  .controls-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
  }

  .control-card {
    padding: var(--kc-space-6);
    background: var(--kc-surface-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--kc-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
  }

  .control-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--kc-charcoal);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-3);
  }

  .control-card p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .protection-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
  }

  .protection-card {
    padding: var(--kc-space-6);
    border: 1px solid var(--kc-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
  }

  .protection-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--kc-charcoal);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-3);
  }

  .protection-card p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .btn--inverse {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--kc-space-4) var(--kc-space-8);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--kc-text-inverse);
    border: 2px solid var(--kc-teal-light);
    transition: all var(--kc-transition-fast);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }

  .btn--inverse:hover {
    background: var(--kc-teal);
    border-color: var(--kc-teal);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .controls-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .protection-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .security-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .page-hero h1 { font-size: var(--kc-text-3xl); }
  }
</style>
